## 8. Pre-rubric impressions (free text)

> Free-form notes. These become inputs to scoring but don't directly
> become scores. Use for context the rubric can't capture.

- `<e.g. "the codebase is well-tested but only in the happy path —
  adversarial test coverage is thin. This won't show up in C6 score
  because coverage is high overall, but it's a real risk.">`
- `<e.g. "the maintainer is responsive on GH issues but the project
  isn't funded — sustainability risk if the downstream consumer adopts this as primary.">`
- `<e.g. "two competing forks have appeared in the last year; community
  is split. Risk of porting the wrong line.">`

